stress-energy-tensor-a8b458b2.symmetry_origin:
This equation is derived from the principle of general covariance, meaning it must be invariant under arbitrary coordinate transformations. This principle is fundamental to Einstein's theory of general relativity. The divergence-free nature of the Einstein tensor (
\nabla^{\mu}G_{\mu\nu} = 0
) ensures that it can be equated to the divergence-free stress-energy tensor (
\nabla^{\mu}T_{\mu\nu} = 0
), which represents the local conservation of energy and momentum in spacetime.

